STOTRA = {
    "deity": "kavya",
    "doc_title": "Meghadūta · Uttaramegha",
    "app_title": "Meghadūta II",
    "h1": "Meghadūta · Uttaramegha",
    "subtitle": "The Cloud Messenger · Part 2: Alakā and the Message (verses 1–55)",
    "note": "The second part of Kālidāsa’s Meghadūta: the city of Alakā, the yakṣa’s house, the wife as the poet imagines her, and the message he sends.",
    "footer": "Source: Sanskrit Wikisource — मेघदूतम् - उत्तरमेघः (public domain); English translation original; editorial notes in SOURCES §10",
    "sections": [
    {'padas': ['vidyudvantaṃ lalitavanitāḥ sendracāpaṃ sacitrāḥ', 'saṅgītāya prahatamurajāḥ snigdhagambhīraghoṣam |', 'antastoyaṃ maṇimayabhuvastuṅgamabhraṃlihāgrāḥ', 'prāsādāstvāṃ tulayitumalaṃ yatra taistairviśeṣaiḥ'], 'num': '|| 1 ||', 'gloss': 'In Alakā the palaces can match you in every particular: you have lightning, they have lovely women; you Indra’s bow, they their paintings; you a deep, soft thunder, they drums struck for music; you water within, they floors of jewels; you are lofty, their tops touch the clouds. |'},
    {'padas': ['haste līlākamalamalake bālakundānuviddhaṃ', 'nītā lodhraprasavarajasā pāṇḍutāmānane śrīḥ |', 'cūḍāpāśe navakuravakaṃ cāru karṇe śirīṣaṃ', 'sīmante ca tvadupagamajaṃ yatra nīpaṃ vadhūnām'], 'num': '|| 2 ||', 'gloss': 'There the women hold a play-lotus in the hand, wear young jasmine twined in the locks, have the beauty of the face made pale with lodhra pollen, a fresh kurubaka in the braid, a graceful śirīṣa at the ear, and in the parting of the hair the kadamba that comes with your arrival. |'},
    {'padas': ['yatronmattabhramaramukharāḥ pādapā nityapuṣpā', 'haṃsaśreṇīracitaraśanā nityapadmā nalinyaḥ |', 'kekotkaṇṭhā bhuvanaśikhino nityabhāsvatkalāpā', 'nityajyotsnāḥ pratihatatamovṛttiramyāḥ pradoṣāḥ'], 'num': '|| 3 ||', 'gloss': 'There the trees are always in flower, loud with maddened bees; the lotus-ponds always in bloom, girdled by rows of swans; the household peacocks, eager, cry out, their tails always shining; the evenings are always moonlit, lovely with the dark driven away. |'},
    {'padas': ['ānandotthaṃ nayanasalilaṃ yatra nānyairnimittai-', 'rnānyastāpaḥ kusumaśarajādiṣṭasaṃyogasādhyāt |', 'nāpyanyasmāt praṇayakalahād viprayogopapatti-', 'rvitteśānāṃ na ca khalu vayo yauvanādanyadasti'], 'num': '|| 4 ||', 'gloss': 'There tears come only from joy; there is no pain but love’s arrows, and that is cured by the longed-for meeting; no parting but from a lovers’ quarrel; and for those wealthy yakṣas there is no age but youth. |'},
    {'padas': ['yasyāṃ yakṣāḥ sitamaṇimayānyetya harmyasthalāni', 'jyotiśchāyākusumaracitānyuttamastrīsahāyāḥ |', 'āsevante madhu ratiphalaṃ kalpavṛkṣaprasūtaṃ', 'tvadgambhīradhvaniṣu śanakaiḥ puṣkareṣvāhateṣu'], 'num': '|| 5 ||', 'gloss': 'There the yakṣas, coming with their fine women to the terraces of white-gem palaces strewn with flowers of starlight, slowly drink the wine borne by the wishing-trees, whose fruit is love, while the drums are struck to the echo of your deep sounds. |'},
    {'padas': ['mandākinyāḥ salilaśiśiraiḥ sevyamānā marudbhi-', 'rmandārāṇāmanutaṭaruhāṃ chāyayā vāritoṣṇāḥ |', 'anveṣṭavyaiḥ kanakasikatāmuṣṭinikṣepagūḍhaiḥ', 'saṃkrīḍante maṇibhiramaraprārthitā yatra kanyāḥ'], 'num': '|| 6 ||', 'gloss': 'There the maidens whom the gods desire, fanned by the winds cool with the water of the Mandākinī, their heat warded off by the shade of the mandāra trees on its bank, play with gems hidden away by throwing handfuls of golden sand, which have to be hunted for. |'},
    {'padas': ['nīvībandhocchvasitaśithilaṃ yatra bimbādharāṇāṃ', 'kṣaumaṃ rāgādanibhṛtakareṣvākṣipatsu priyeṣu |', 'arcistuṅgānabhimukhamapi prāpya ratnapradīpān', 'hrīmūḍhānāṃ bhavati viphalapreraṇā cūrṇamuṣṭiḥ'], 'num': '|| 7 ||', 'gloss': 'There, when their lovers in passion tug with restless hands at the silk of women with bimba-red lips, loosened as the knot of the waist-cord slips, the girls, dazed with shyness, fling handfuls of powder at the jewel-lamps — in vain: even reaching the high flames, they do not put them out. |'},
    {'padas': ['netrā nītāḥ satatagatinā yadvimānāgrabhūmī-', 'rālekhyānāṃ salilakaṇikādoṣamutpādya sadyaḥ |', 'śaṅkāspṛṣṭā iva jalamucastvādṛśā jālamārgai-', 'rdhūmodgārānukṛtinipuṇā jarjarā niṣpatanti'], 'num': '|| 8 ||', 'gloss': 'There clouds like you, led by the ever-moving wind to the upper floors of the mansions, spoil the paintings at once with drops of water and then, as if touched by fear, slip out through the lattices, shredded and clever at imitating smoke. |'},
    {'padas': ['yatra strīṇāṃ priyatamabhujocchvāsitāliṅgitānām', 'aṅgaglāniṃ suratajanitāṃ tantujālāvalambāḥ |', 'tvatsaṃrodhāpagamaviśadaścandrapādairniśīthe', 'vyālumpanti sphuṭajalalavasyandinaścandrakāntāḥ'], 'num': '|| 9 ||', 'gloss': 'There the moonstones, hanging from nets of thread, brighten in the moonbeams at midnight, once you have stopped blocking them, and by dripping clear drops of water take away the weariness of love from the limbs of women embraced by their lovers’ arms. |'},
    {'padas': ['akṣayyāntarbhavananidhayaḥ pratyahaṃ raktakaṇṭhai-', 'rudgāyadbhirdhanapatiyaśaḥ kiṃnarairyatra sārdham |', 'vaibhrājākhyaṃ vibudhavanitāvāramukhyāsahāyā', 'baddhālāpā bahirupavanaṃ kāmino nirviśanti'], 'num': '|| 10 ||', 'gloss': 'There lovers, with inexhaustible treasures in their houses, enjoy themselves, talking together, in the outer garden called Vaibhrāja, in company with the finest of the heavenly courtesans, while Kinnaras with rich red throats sing every day the glory of the lord of wealth. |'},
    {'padas': ['gatyutkampādalakapatitairyatra mandārapuṣpaiḥ', 'putracchedaiḥ kanakakamalaiḥ karṇavisraṃsibhiśca |', 'muktājālaiḥ stanaparisaracchinnasūtraiśca hārai-', 'rnaiśo mārgaḥ saviturudaye sūcyate kāminīnām'], 'num': '|| 11 ||', 'gloss': 'There the night road of the women is shown at sunrise by mandāra flowers fallen from their hair in their hurry, by leaf-ornaments, by golden lotuses slipped from their ears, by nets of pearls, and by necklaces whose threads are broken about the breasts. |'},
    {'padas': ['vāsaścitraṃ madhu nayanayorvibhramādeśadakṣaṃ', 'puṣpodbhedaṃ saha kisalayairbhūṣaṇānāṃ vikalpam |', 'lākṣārāgaṃ caraṇakamalanyāsayogyaṃ ca yasyām', 'ekaḥ sūte sakalamabalāmaṇḍanaṃ kalpavṛkṣaḥ'], 'num': '|| 12 ||', 'gloss': 'There one wishing-tree alone bears all the ornaments of women: garments of many colours, the wine that teaches the eyes their sidelong play, flowers with shoots, a choice of jewels, and lac-dye fit for the setting down of lotus feet. |'},
    {'padas': ['patraśyāmā dinakarahayaspardhino yatra vāhāḥ', 'śailodagrāstvamiva kariṇo vṛṣṭimantaḥ prabhedāt |', 'yodhāgraṇyaḥ pratidaśamukhaṃ saṃyuge tasthivāṃsaḥ', 'pratyādiṣṭābharaṇarucayaścandrahāsavraṇāṅkaiḥ'], 'num': '|| 13 ||', 'gloss': 'There the horses, dark as leaves, rival the sun’s steeds; the elephants, tall as mountains, give rain from their rut as you do; and the foremost warriors, who stand in battle against any ten-headed foe, have no taste for ornaments, for the scars of the Candrahāsa sword are enough. |'},
    {'padas': ['matvā devaṃ dhanapatisakhaṃ yatra sākṣād vasantaṃ', 'prāyaścāpaṃ na vahati bhayānmanmathaḥ ṣaṭpadajyam |', 'sabhrūbhaṅgaprahitanayanaiḥ kāmilakṣyeṣvamoghai-', 'stasyārambhaścaturavanitāvibhramaireva siddhaḥ'], 'num': '|| 14 ||', 'gloss': 'There Kāma, thinking that the friend of the lord of wealth lives there in person, for fear mostly does not carry his bow strung with bees; yet his work is done by the clever women’s play of glances with knitted brows, which never miss their marks, the lovers. |'},
    {'padas': ['tatrāgāraṃ dhanapatigṛhānuttareṇāsmadīyaṃ', 'dūrāllakṣyaṃ surapatidhanuścāruṇā toraṇena |', 'yasyopānte kṛtakatanayaḥ kāntayā vardhito me', 'hastaprāpyastabakanamito bālamandāravṛkṣaḥ'], 'num': '|| 15 ||', 'gloss': 'There, north of the lord of wealth’s palace, is my house, easily seen from afar by its lovely arched gateway like Indra’s bow; beside it stands a young mandāra tree that my wife reared as a son, bent down by clusters of flowers within reach of the hand. |'},
    {'padas': ['vāpī cāsmin marakataśilābaddhasopānamārgā', 'haimaiśchannā vikacakamalaiḥ snigdhavaidūryanālaiḥ |', 'yasyāstoye kṛtavasatayo mānasaṃ saṃnikṛṣṭaṃ', 'nādhyāsyanti vyapagataśucastvāmapi prekṣya haṃsāḥ'], 'num': '|| 16 ||', 'gloss': 'In the house is a pond with steps of emerald slabs, covered with golden lotuses in bloom on glossy lapis stems; the swans that live in its water, free from sorrow, will not even long for nearby Mānasa when they see you. |'},
    {'padas': ['tasyāstīre racitaśikharaḥ peśalairindranīlaiḥ', 'krīḍāśailaḥ kanakakadalīveṣṭanaprekṣaṇīyaḥ |', 'madgehinyāḥ priya iti sakhe cetasā kātareṇa', 'prekṣyopāntasphuritataḍitaṃ tvāṃ tameva smarāmi'], 'num': '|| 17 ||', 'gloss': 'On its bank is a pleasure-hill, its peak made of soft sapphires, lovely to see with its ring of golden plantains; it is dear to my wife, friend, and with an anxious heart I remember it when I see you with lightning flickering at your edge. |'},
    {'padas': ['raktāśokaścalakisalayaḥ kesaraścātra kāntaḥ', 'pratyāsannau kuruvakavṛtermādhavīmaṇḍapasya |', 'ekaḥ sakhyāstava saha mayā vāmapādābhilāṣī', 'kāṅkṣatyanyo vadanamadirāṃ dohadacchadmanāsyāḥ'], 'num': '|| 18 ||', 'gloss': 'There a red aśoka with trembling shoots and a lovely kesara tree stand close to the arbour of jasmine fenced with kurubaka; the one, like your friend, longs with me for the touch of her left foot; the other, under the pretext of a pregnancy-craving, wants the wine of her mouth. |'},
    {'padas': ['tanmadhye ca sphaṭikaphalakā kāñcanī vāsayaṣṭi-', 'rmūle baddhā maṇibhiranatiprauḍhavaṃśaprakāśaiḥ |', 'tālaiḥ śiñjāvalayasubhagairnartitaḥ kāntayā me', 'yāmadhyāste divasavigame nīlakaṇṭhaḥ suhṛdvaḥ'], 'num': '|| 19 ||', 'gloss': 'Between them stands a golden perch with a crystal slab, its base set with gems bright as young bamboo; there at the day’s end sits your friend the blue-throated peacock, whom my wife makes dance to the claps of hands whose bracelets tinkle sweetly. |'},
    {'padas': ['ebhiḥ sādho hṛdayanihitairlakṣaṇairlakṣayethā', 'dvāropānte likhitavapuṣau śaṅkhapadmau ca dṛṣṭvā |', 'kṣāmacchāyāṃ bhavanamadhunā madviyogena nūnaṃ', 'sūryāpāye na khalu kamalaṃ puṣyati svāmabhikhyām'], 'num': '|| 20 ||', 'gloss': 'By these marks, laid up in your heart, good one, you will know it; and also by seeing at the door the conch and the lotus painted there. Without me the house now surely has a faded look; at sunset the lotus does not keep its beauty. |'},
    {'padas': ['gatvā sadyaḥ kalabhatanutāṃ śīghrasaṃpātahetoḥ', 'krīḍāśaile prathamakathite ramyasānau niṣaṇṇaḥ |', 'arhasyantarbhavanapatitāṃ kartumalpālpabhāsaṃ', 'khadyotālīvilasitanibhāṃ vidyudunmeṣadṛṣṭim'], 'num': '|| 21 ||', 'gloss': 'Becoming at once the size of an elephant calf, to make a swift descent, settle on the lovely slope of the pleasure-hill I first spoke of; you can make your lightning, fallen inside the house, give a faint light, like the glimmer of a row of fireflies. |'},
    {'padas': ['tanvī śyāmā śikharidaśanā pakvabimbādharoṣṭhī', 'madhye kṣāmā cakitahariṇīprekṣaṇā nimnanābhiḥ |', 'śroṇībhārādalasagamanā stokanamrā stanābhyāṃ', 'yā tatra syādyuvativiṣaye sṛṣṭirādyeva dhātuḥ'], 'num': '|| 22 ||', 'gloss': 'Slender, dark, with fine pointed teeth and lips red as ripe bimba fruit, thin in the waist, with the glance of a startled doe, deep in the navel, slow of gait from the weight of her hips, a little bowed by her breasts — she who is there is the Creator’s first work among women. |'},
    {'padas': ['tāṃ jānīthāḥ parimitakathāṃ jīvitaṃ me dvitīyaṃ', 'dūrībhūte mayi sahacare cakravākīmivaikām |', 'gāḍhotkaṇṭhāṃ guruṣu divaseṣveṣu gacchatsu bālāṃ', 'jātāṃ manye śiśiramathitāṃ padminīṃ vānyarūpām'], 'num': '|| 23 ||', 'gloss': 'Know her, sparing of words, as my second life, like a lone cakravāka hen when her mate is far away; I think that, as these heavy days pass, the young wife, deep in longing, has been changed, like a lotus-plant struck by frost. |'},
    {'padas': ['nūnaṃ tasyāḥ prabalaruditocchūnanetraṃ priyāyā', 'niḥśvāsānāmaśiśiratayā bhinnavarṇādharoṣṭham |', 'hastanyastaṃ mukhamasakalavyakti lambālakatvād', 'indordainyaṃ tvadanusaraṇakliṣṭakānterbibharti'], 'num': '|| 24 ||', 'gloss': 'Surely my beloved has eyes swollen from violent weeping, her lower lip discoloured by the heat of her sighs, her face, half-hidden by her long hanging hair, resting in her hand; she wears the dejection of the moon, its brightness dimmed as you follow it. |'},
    {'padas': ['āloke te nipatati purā sā balivyākulā vā', 'matsādṛśyaṃ virahatanu vā bhāvagamyaṃ likhantī |', 'pṛcchantī vā madhuravacanāṃ sārikāṃ pañjarasthāṃ', 'kaccid bhartuḥ smarasi rasike tvaṃ hi tasya priyeti'], 'num': '|| 25 ||', 'gloss': 'When you come into her sight she will be busy either with the offering, or drawing my likeness, thin with parting, as she imagines me; or asking the sweet-voiced mynah in its cage, “Do you remember your master, clever one? You were his favourite.” |'},
    {'padas': ['utsaṅge vā malinavasane saumya nikṣipya vīṇāṃ', 'madgotrāṅkaṃ viracitapadaṃ geyamudgātukāmā |', 'tantrīmārdrāṃ nayanasalilaiḥ sārayitvā kathaṃcid', 'bhūyo bhūyaḥ svayamapi kṛtāṃ mūrcchanāṃ vismarantī'], 'num': '|| 26 ||', 'gloss': 'Or, gentle one, she will have laid the lute on her soiled skirt and want to sing a song with my name worked into its words; having somehow wiped the strings, wet with her tears, she forgets again and again the tune she herself composed. |'},
    {'padas': ['śeṣān māsān virahadivasasthāpitasyāvadhervā', 'vinyasyantī bhuvi gaṇanayā dehalīdattapuṣpaiḥ |', 'sambhogaṃ vā hṛdayanihitārambhamāsvādayantī', 'prāyeṇaite ramaṇaviraheṣvaṅganānāṃ vinodāḥ'], 'num': '|| 27 ||', 'gloss': 'Or she lays flowers on the threshold, counting on the ground the months that remain of the term set at the start of our parting; or she tastes in her heart the union she longs for. These are mostly the pastimes of women when their husbands are away. |'},
    {'padas': ['savyāpārāmahani na tathā pīḍayed viprayogaḥ', 'śaṅke rātrau gurutaraśucaṃ nirvinodāṃ sakhīṃ te |', 'matsandeśaḥ sukhayitumalaṃ paśya sādhvīṃ niśīthe', 'tāmunnidrāmavaniśayanāṃ saudhavātāyanasthaḥ'], 'num': '|| 28 ||', 'gloss': 'In the daytime, being busy, she will not be so tormented by separation; I fear for your friend at night, heavier in grief and without distraction. Standing at the lattice of the palace, look at that faithful one sleepless on her bed on the ground at midnight; my message can bring her comfort. |'},
    {'padas': ['ādhikṣāmāṃ virahaśayane saṃniṣaṇṇaikapārśvāṃ', 'prācīmūle tanumiva kalāmātraśeṣāṃ himāṃśoḥ |', 'nītā rātriḥ kṣaṇa iva mayā sārdhamicchāratairyā', 'tāmevoṣṇairvirahamahatīmaśrubhiryāpayantīm'], 'num': '|| 29 ||', 'gloss': 'Wasted by grief, lying on one side on the bed of separation, like the thin sliver of the moon left at the foot of the eastern sky — she who passed the night with me in a moment, in the pleasures of love, now spends it, made long by parting, in hot tears. |'},
    {'padas': ['pādānindoramṛtaśiśirāñjālamārgapraviṣṭān', 'pūrvaprītyā gatamabhimukhaṃ saṃnivṛttaṃ tathaiva |', 'cakṣuḥ khedāt salilagurubhiḥ pakṣmabhiśchādayantīṃ', "sābhre'hnīva sthalakamalinī naprabuddhāṃ nasuptām"], 'num': '|| 30 ||', 'gloss': 'She covers with lashes heavy with water the eye which, from old affection, went toward the moon’s rays, cool as nectar, coming through the lattice, and then turned away again; she is neither awake nor asleep, like a land-lotus on a cloudy day. |'},
    {'padas': ['niḥśvāsenādharakisalayakleśinā vikṣipantīṃ', 'śuddhasnānātparuṣamalakaṃ nūnamāgaṇḍalambam |', "matsaṃbhogaḥ kathamupanametsvapnajo'pīti nidrām", 'ākāṅkṣantīṃ nayanasalilotpīḍaruddhāvakāśam'], 'num': '|| 31 ||', 'gloss': 'With a sigh that torments her lip like a shoot she thrusts back her hair, rough from a bath without oil, hanging down to her cheek; she longs for sleep, thinking “may union with me come, even in a dream,” but tears pressing from her eyes leave it no room. |'},
    {'padas': ['ādye baddhā virahadivase yā śikhā dāma hitvā', 'śāpasyānte vigalitaśucā tāṃ mayodveṣṭanīyām |', 'sparśakliṣṭāmayamitanakhenāsakṛtsārayantīṃ', 'gaṇḍābhogāt kaṭhinaviṣamāmekaveṇīṃ kareṇa'], 'num': '|| 32 ||', 'gloss': 'The single braid she bound on the first day of our parting, putting aside the garland, which I am to loosen when the curse is over and the sorrow gone — she pushes it from her cheek again and again with a hand whose nails are untrimmed and hurt at its touch, the braid hard and tangled. |'},
    {'padas': ['sā saṃnyastābharaṇamabalā peśalaṃ dhārayantī', 'śayyotsaṅge nihitamasakṛd duḥkhaduḥkhena gātram |', 'tvāmapyasraṃ navajalamayaṃ mocayiṣyatyavaśyaṃ', 'prāyaḥ sarvo bhavati karuṇāvṛttirārdrāntarātmā'], 'num': '|| 33 ||', 'gloss': 'That frail woman, having laid aside her ornaments, her delicate body set down on the bed with pain upon pain, will surely make even you let fall tears of fresh water; for almost everyone whose heart is moist is moved to compassion. |'},
    {'padas': ['jāne sakhyāstava mayi manaḥ saṃbhṛtasnehamasmād', 'itthaṃbhūtāṃ prathamavirahe tāmahaṃ tarkayāmi |', 'vācālaṃ māṃ na khalu subhagaṃmanyabhāvaḥ karoti', 'pratyakṣaṃ te nikhilamacirād bhrātaruktaṃ mayā yat'], 'num': '|| 34 ||', 'gloss': 'I know that your friend’s heart is full of love for me; so I picture her thus in this, our first parting. It is not conceit of being fortunate that makes me talk so much; what I have said, brother, you will see before your eyes before long. |'},
    {'padas': ['ruddhāpāṅgaprasarama alakairañjanasnehaśūnyaṃ', 'pratyādeśādapi ca madhuno vismṛtabhrūvilāsam |', 'tvayyāsanne nayanamuparispandi śaṅke mṛgākṣyā', 'mīnakṣobhācalakuvalayaśrītulāmeṣyatīti'], 'num': '|| 35 ||', 'gloss': 'I fear that the eye of the doe-eyed one, its sideways reach blocked by her hair, deprived of the oil of collyrium, its play of brows forgotten since she gave up wine, will, when you draw near, twitch upward and match the beauty of a blue lotus stirred by a leaping fish. |'},
    {'padas': ['vāmaścāsyāḥ kararuhapadairmucyamāno madīyai-', 'rmuktājālaṃ ciraparicitaṃ tyājito daivagatyā |', 'sambhogānte mama samucito hastasaṃvāhamānāṃ', 'yāsyatyūruḥ sarasakadalīstambhagauraścalatvam'], 'num': '|| 36 ||', 'gloss': 'Her left thigh, pale as the trunk of a fresh plantain, once marked by my nails, and now by the turn of fate deprived of the pearl-girdle it wore so long, which used to know the rubbing of my hand at the end of love, will tremble. |'},
    {'padas': ['tasmin kāle jalada yadi sā labdhanidrāsukhā syād', 'anvāsyaināṃ stanitavimukho yāmamātraṃ sahasva |', 'mā bhūdasyāḥ praṇayini mayi svapnalabdhe kathañcit', 'sadyaḥ kaṇṭhacyutabhujalatāgranthi gāḍhopagūḍham'], 'num': '|| 37 ||', 'gloss': 'At that time, cloud, if she has found the comfort of sleep, wait beside her and bear to hold back your thunder for one watch of the night; let her not lose at once, when she has somehow got me in a dream, the embrace in which the creepers of my arms were tight around her neck. |'},
    {'padas': ['tāmutthāpya svajalakaṇikāśītalenānilena', 'pratyāśvastāṃ samamabhinavairjālakairmālatīnām |', 'vidyudgarbhaḥ stimitanayanāṃ tvatsanāthe gavākṣe', 'vaktuṃ dhīraḥ stanitavacanairmāninīṃ prakramethāḥ'], 'num': '|| 38 ||', 'gloss': 'Having woken her with a breeze cool from your drops, and refreshed her along with the fresh jasmine buds, then, with lightning held in your womb, and her eyes steady at the window you now share, begin boldly to speak to the proud woman in words of thunder. |'},
    {'padas': ['bharturmitraṃ priyamavidhave viddhi māmambuvāhaṃ', 'tatsandeśairhṛdayanihitairāgataṃ tvatsamīpam |', 'yo vṛndāni tvarayati pathi śramyatāṃ proṣitānāṃ', 'mandrasnigdhairdhvanibhirabalāveṇimokṣotsukāni'], 'num': '|| 39 ||', 'gloss': '“Know me, O woman whose husband lives, as the friend of your husband, a cloud, come near you with his message laid in my heart — I who with deep and soft sounds hurry the troops of weary travellers, eager to loosen their wives’ braids.” |'},
    {'padas': ['ityākhyāte pavanatanayaṃ maithilīvonmukhī sā', 'tvāmutkaṇṭhocchvasitahṛdayā vīkṣya sambhāvya caiva |', 'śroṣyatyasmāt paramavahitā saumya sīmantinīnāṃ', 'kāntodantaḥ suhṛdupanataḥ saṅgamāt kiṃcidūnaḥ'], 'num': '|| 40 ||', 'gloss': 'Told so, she will look up at you, as Maithilī at the wind’s son, her heart swelling with longing, and she will see you and welcome you, and listen most attentively; for the news of her beloved brought by a friend, gentle one, is for women but a little less than meeting him. |'},
    {'padas': ['tāmāyuṣman mama ca vacanādātmanaścopakartuṃ', 'brūyā evaṃ tava sahacaro rāmagiryāśramasthaḥ |', 'avyāpannaḥ kuśalamabale pṛcchati tvāṃ viyuktaḥ', 'pūrvābhāṣyaṃ sulabhavipadāṃ prāṇināmetadeva'], 'num': '|| 41 ||', 'gloss': 'Then, long-lived one, to do her a kindness, say to her, both in my words and your own: “Your companion, who lives in the hermitage of Rāmagiri, is unharmed and, parted from you, asks after your welfare.” This is the first thing to say to creatures whose troubles come easily. |'},
    {'padas': ['aṅgenāṅgaṃ pratanu tanunā gāḍhataptena taptaṃ', 'sāsreṇāśrudrutamaviratotkaṇṭhamutkaṇṭhitena |', 'uṣṇocchvāsaṃ samadhikatarocchvāsinā dūravartī', 'saṃkalpaistairviśati vidhinā vairiṇā ruddhamārgaḥ'], 'num': '|| 42 ||', 'gloss': '“Far away, his road barred by hostile fate, he comes to you in fancy: his thin body to your thinner limbs, burning deep to you burning, tearful to your tears, longing without pause to your longing, hot sigh to your sigh, which is heavier still.” |'},
    {'padas': ['śabdākhyeyaṃ yadapi kila te yaḥ sakhīnāṃ purastāt', 'karṇe lolaḥ kathayitumabhūdānanasparśalobhāt |', "so'tikrāntaḥ śravaṇaviṣayaṃ locanābhyāmadṛṣṭa-", 'stvāmutkaṇṭhāviracitapadaṃ manmukhenedamāha'], 'num': '|| 43 ||', 'gloss': '“What could be spoken in words, which he, eager, in front of your friends would try to say into your ear for greed of touching your face — he has gone beyond hearing and is hidden from your eyes, and so he speaks to you by my mouth, in words made by longing.” |'},
    {'padas': ['śyāmāsvaṅgaṃ cakitahariṇīprekṣaṇe dṛṣṭipātaṃ', 'vaktracchāyāṃ śaśini śikhināṃ barhabhāreṣu keśān |', 'utpaśyāmi pratanuṣu nadīvīciṣu bhrūvilāsān', 'hantaikasmin kvacidapi na te caṇḍi sādṛśyamasti'], 'num': '|| 44 ||', 'gloss': '“In the priyaṅgu creepers I see your limbs, in the startled doe your glance, in the moon the lustre of your face, in the peacocks’ plumage your hair, in the thin ripples of the river your play of brows; but alas, fierce one, nowhere do I find all of you together.” |'},
    {'padas': ['tvāmālikhya praṇayakupitāṃ dhāturāgaiḥ śilāyām', 'ātmānaṃ te caraṇapatitaṃ yāvadicchāmi kartum |', 'asraistāvanmuhurupacitairdṛṣṭirālupyate me', 'krūrastasminnapi na sahate saṅgamaṃ nau kṛtāntaḥ'], 'num': '|| 45 ||', 'gloss': '“When I paint you on a rock in mineral colours, angry with love, and then try to paint myself fallen at your feet, tears welling again and again blot out my sight; even there cruel fate cannot bear our meeting.” |'},
    {'padas': ['dhārāsiktasthalasurabhiṇasstvanmukhasyāsya bāle', 'dūrībhūtaṃ pratanumapi māṃ pañcabāṇaḥ kṣiṇoti |', "gharmānte'smin vigaṇaya kathaṃ vāsarāṇi vrajeyu-", 'rdiksaṃsaktapravitataghanavyastasūryātapāni'], 'num': '|| 45a ||', 'gloss': '“Far from your face, girl, fragrant as earth sprinkled with showers, the god of the five arrows torments me, though I am thin already. Think how these days at the end of summer will pass, with the sun’s heat scattered by clouds spread across the quarters.” (This verse is not in all manuscripts, and its text is uncertain.) |'},
    {'padas': ['māmākāśapraṇihitabhujaṃ nirdayāśleṣaheto-', 'rlabdhāyāste kathamapi mayā svapnasandarśaneṣu |', 'paśyantīnāṃ na khalu bahuśo na sthalīdevatānāṃ', 'muktāsthūlāstarukisalayeṣvaśruleśāḥ patanti'], 'num': '|| 46 ||', 'gloss': '“When I somehow get you in my dreams, and stretch out my arms into the air to embrace you, the goddesses of the place who watch me often let fall tears as big as pearls on the tree-shoots.” |'},
    {'padas': ['bhittvā sadyaḥ kisalayapuṭān devadārudrumāṇāṃ', 'ye tatkṣīrasrutisurabhayo dakṣiṇena pravṛttāḥ |', 'āliṅgyante guṇavati mayā te tuṣārādrivātāḥ', 'pūrvaṃ spṛṣṭaṃ yadi kila bhavedaṅgamebhistaveti'], 'num': '|| 47 ||', 'gloss': '“Those winds from the Snow Mountain that blow from the south, splitting at once the shoot-sheaths of the deodar trees, fragrant with their sap, I embrace, virtuous one, thinking that perhaps they touched your limbs before.” |'},
    {'padas': ['saṃkṣipyeta kṣaṇa iva kathaṃ dīrghayāmā triyāmā', 'sarvāvasthāsvaharapi kathaṃ mandamandātapaṃ syāt |', 'itthaṃ cetaścaṭulanayane durlabhaprārthanaṃ me', 'gāḍhoṣmābhiḥ kṛtamaśaraṇaṃ tvadviyogavyathābhiḥ'], 'num': '|| 48 ||', 'gloss': '“How can the three-watch night be shortened to a moment? How can the day be mild in its heat in every state? So, restless-eyed one, my mind, with wishes so hard to fulfil, is left helpless by the pangs of parting from you, hot to the core.” |'},
    {'padas': ['nanvātmānaṃ bahu vigaṇayannātmanaivāvalambe', 'tatkalyāṇi tvamapi nitarāṃ mā gamaḥ kātaratvam |', 'kasyātyantaṃ sukhamupanataṃ duḥkhamekāntato vā', 'nīcairgacchatyupari ca daśā cakranemikrameṇa'], 'num': '|| 49 ||', 'gloss': '“I sustain myself by my own thoughts, counting myself fortunate; you too, auspicious one, must not fall into utter dejection. Whose happiness is unbroken, or whose sorrow is wholly unrelieved? Our condition goes down and up like the rim of a wheel.” |'},
    {'padas': ['śāpānto me bhujagaśayanādutthite śārṅgapāṇau', 'śeṣān māsān gamaya caturo locane mīlayitvā |', 'paścādāvāṃ virahaguṇitaṃ taṃ tamātmābhilāṣaṃ', 'nirvekṣyāvaḥ pariṇataśaraccandrikāsu kṣapāsu'], 'num': '|| 50 ||', 'gloss': '“My curse ends when the bearer of the Śārṅga bow rises from his serpent-bed; pass the four months that remain with your eyes shut. Afterwards we shall both enjoy every wish, multiplied by our parting, in the nights of ripened autumn moonlight.” |'},
    {'padas': ['bhūyaścāha tvamapi śayane kaṇṭhalagnā purā me', 'nidrāṃ gatvā kimapi rudatī sasvaraṃ viprabuddhā |', 'sāntarhāsaṃ kathitamasakṛt pṛcchataśca tvayā me', 'dṛṣṭaḥ svapne kitava ramayan kāmapi tvaṃ mayeti'], 'num': '|| 51 ||', 'gloss': '“And he said again: ‘Once, as you lay in bed with your arms about my neck, you fell asleep and then woke up weeping aloud; when I asked and asked, you said, laughing inwardly: “In a dream, deceiver, I saw you making love to some woman!”’” |'},
    {'padas': ['etasmānmāṃ kuśalinamabhijñānadānād viditvā', 'mā kaulīnādasitanayane mayyaviśvāsinī bhūḥ |', 'snehānāhuḥ kimapi virahe dhvaṃsinaste tvabhogād', 'iṣṭe vastunyupacitarasāḥ premarāśībhavanti'], 'num': '|| 52 ||', 'gloss': '“By this token know that I am well, and, dark-eyed one, do not mistrust me because of gossip. They say love is destroyed in separation, but love, deprived of enjoyment, gathers its sweetness for the thing desired and becomes a heap of affection.” |'},
    {'padas': ['āśvāsyaivaṃ prathamavirahodagraśokāṃ sakhīṃ te', 'śailādāśu trinayanavṛṣotkhātakūṭānnivṛttaḥ |', 'sābhijñānaprahitakuśalaistatadvacobhirmamāpi', 'prātaḥ kundaprasavaśithilaṃ jīvitaṃ dhārayethāḥ'], 'num': '|| 53 ||', 'gloss': '“Having comforted your friend in this way, her grief keen in this first parting, return quickly from that mountain whose peak the bull of the three-eyed god tore up, and sustain my life, loose as a jasmine flower at dawn, with her words in answer, bringing news of her welfare and carrying a token.” |'},
    {'padas': ['kaccit saumya vyavasitamidaṃ bandhukṛtyaṃ tvayā me', 'pratyādeśānna khalu bhavato dhīratāṃ kalpayāmi |', "niḥśabdo'pi pradiśasi jalaṃ yācitaścātakebhyaḥ", 'pratyuktaṃ hi praṇayiṣu satāmīpsitārthakriyaiva'], 'num': '|| 54 ||', 'gloss': '“Gentle one, will you do this kindness for a friend? I do not take your silence for a refusal, for I think you steadfast; you give water to the cātakas when they ask, though without a word; for the good, the answer to those who ask is to do what is wanted.” |'},
    {'padas': ['etatkṛtvā priyamanucitaprārthanāvartino me', 'sauhārdādvā vidhura iti vā mayyanukrośabuddhyā |', 'iṣṭāndeśāñjalada vicara prāvṛṣā saṃbhṛtaśrī-', 'rmā bhūdevaṃ kṣaṇamapi ca te vidyutā viprayogaḥ'], 'num': '|| 55 ||', 'gloss': '“Having done this kindness for me, though my request was improper, whether out of friendship or out of pity for me, bereft, go, cloud, to whatever lands you please, your beauty swollen by the rains; and may you never be parted, even for a moment, from your lightning.” |'},
    ],
}
